@startuml
title Recording dedupe and representative selection — v4

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

control "Queue Consumer" as Consumer
participant "Spotify Web API" as Spotify
database "D1 recordings\n(private staging)" as D1

== Identity ==

Consumer -> Spotify: GET /v1/tracks/{id} (full object)\n≤30 reads per queue delivery, ≤5 concurrent
Spotify --> Consumer: Tracks with external_ids.isrc,\nrelease dates, artwork, credits

Consumer -> Consumer: Normalize the ISRC\n(strip separators, uppercase; invalid → none)
Consumer -> Consumer: recording_key =\nisrc:ISRC when confirmed, else spotify:{id}

note right of Consumer
  Different pressings, singles, and re-issues of
  one song usually share an ISRC and collapse
  into a single recording. Without a confirmed
  ISRC the exact Spotify id is the identity.
end note

== Eligibility ==

Consumer -> Consumer: Keep only strictly playable tracks:\nSpotify affirms is_playable, not is_local,\nand id/name/album/first artist/URL present

== Dedupe and representative choice ==

Consumer -> Consumer: Group survivors by recording_key
loop Each recording group
  Consumer -> Consumer: Pick one representative:\n1. earliest release date\n   (partial dates order before later ones;\n   unknown or malformed dates sort last)\n2. then prefer having artwork\n3. then the smaller Spotify id
  Consumer -> D1: INSERT OR IGNORE the representative row\n(recording_key, spotify_id, isrc, title, album,\nrelease_date, image_url, ordered artists_json,\nbucket_artist_id = first credited artist)
end

Consumer -> D1: Staged rows are private:\nno live_generation points here yet

note over Consumer,D1 #D9EAD3
  The bucket artist is the first credited artist of the
  representative. It drives the uniform artist draw of
  the public recommendation (flow 07), so a prolific
  artist cannot flood the shelf relative to a sparse one.
end note

@enduml
